# One-Pot Orzo with Sausage, Spinach, and Corn

Based on [https://www.skinnytaste.com/one-pot-orzo-with-sausage-spinach-and-corn/…](https://www.skinnytaste.com/one-pot-orzo-with-sausage-spinach-and-corn/#recipe) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250703090608/https://www.skinnytaste.com/one-pot-orzo-with-sausage-spinach-and-corn/))

{ rating="5" image="one_pot_orzo_with_sausage_spinach_and_corn.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Pot

- [ ] 12-16 ounces [sausage]{ ing="sausage" }
- [ ] 2/3 medium [yellow onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, chopped
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1 can [corn]{ ing="corn" }, drained
- [ ] 1 can [diced tomatoes]{ ing="diced-tomatoes" }, with liquid
- [ ] 1 tsp [Italian or similar seasoning]{ ing="italian-or-similar-seasoning" }
- [ ] 1 cup [dry orzo]{ ing="dry-orzo" }
- [ ] 3 cups [low sodium chicken broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" }
- [ ] [frozen peas]{ ing="frozen-peas" }
- [ ] (Optional) toss in up to a few handfuls of [spinach to wilt]{ ing="spinach-to-wilt" } in the last few minutes

### Serving

- [ ] 1/4 cup freshly [grated Parmesan]{ ing="grated-parmesan" }
- [ ] [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] [Optionally add Zucchini]{ ing="optionally-add-zucchini" } or other vegetables with the peas

## Recipe

1. Remove the [sausage]{ ing="sausage" } from the casing, break up, and cook in a Dutch oven for 5 minutes on medium-high heat
1. Add the [onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" } and saute until golden (~5 min)
1. Add the [corn]{ ing="corn" } and [tomatoes]{ ing="diced-tomatoes" } and cook until reduced (~10 min)
1. Add the [orzo]{ ing="dry-orzo" }, [chicken broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" }, [frozen peas]{ ing="frozen-peas" }, and any additional [seasonings]{ ing="italian-or-similar-seasoning" }, stir to combine then bring to a boil. Stir and scrape the bottom to keep orzo from sticking
1. Reduce heat to medium-low and simmer 10 minutes
1. Top with freshly [grated Parmesan]{ ing="grated-parmesan" } and [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }

